# Old project-keyed URLs -> new SaaS-keyed URLs (Cloudflare Workers static
# assets honor this file, same as public/_headers).
#
# FORMAT: one rule per line, `<from> <to> <status>`. Paths only, no host.
# Blank lines and `#` comments are ignored. Rules are evaluated in order and the
# first match wins, so nothing here may overlap. Cloudflare's limit is 2,100
# static rules; we are nowhere near it.
#
# WHY: the site used to ask its question about the free app — /self-host/
# excalidraw/. It now asks about the paid one — /self-host/miro/ — so every
# project URL that was indexed, linked, or pasted into somebody's notes is gone.
# A 301 is the only thing that carries the accumulated links across. These are
# permanent: the old URLs are never coming back under a different meaning.
#
# DERIVED FROM DATA, NOT TYPED: for every SaaS page (data/saas/*.json with a
# non-empty `ranked`), every ranked option whose project slug differs from the
# SaaS slug gets two rules — the HTML page and its .md mirror. Order follows
# getAllSaasPages(): primary.pagePriority, then SaaS name.
#
# REGENERATE THIS FILE WHENEVER A PAIRING CHANGES. Adding a SaaS entity,
# re-ranking `ranked` so a different project is primary, renaming a project or
# SaaS slug, or retiring a project all change the correct contents here, and
# nothing fails if you forget — the stale rule just quietly sends readers to the
# wrong page, or to a 404, which is exactly the failure a redirect exists to
# prevent. Two rules per pair; 10 pairs today.

